+# Repair status against A1–A7 and B1–B16
+
+This repairs ORIGINAL using reviewed REFERENCE ideas. It does not claim every problem is solved. The ORIGINAL frontend is frozen byte-for-byte, all ten edge classes remain, and the input still has 56 features. The historical reference audit is `sih26073_code_audit.md`; this file describes the delivered state. Measured numbers and commands are in `docs/EVALUATION.md`, generated from the included JSON artifacts.
+
+`Fixed (software)` means relevant software evidence exists; it does not certify ESP32 hardware. `Partial` identifies remaining requirements or measurements. `Needs hardware` means implementation exists but physical behavior is unverified.
+
+| Finding | Status | Implementation and evidence | Remaining limitation |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| A1: SPIKE label noise | Fixed (software) | `corpus.py` labels altered transient samples only and persistent intervals until recovery, then NORMAL. Label tests pass. `ablate_spike_labels.py` fits five models with the old training-label bug on identical raw sessions; controlled results are in `label_ablation_metrics.json`. | Independent labels are still required for field records. |
+| A2: tiny/leaky test set | Fixed (software) | `train_edge_mlp.py` uses complete sessions, five seeds, disjoint split namespaces, manifests, mean and sample SD. Final test has 32 sessions per class per seed. Contract tests check split disjointness. | SD is across seeds, not a confidence interval over correlated observations. |
+| A3: unrealistic synthetic data | Partial | `corpus.py` adds varying noise/levels, diurnal phase, NORMAL weather fronts, quantized humidity, five installed-sensor profiles and ambiguous normal controls. | Broader coverage does not establish realism; field weather and sensor-specific fault distributions need data. |
+| A4: FROZEN onset/plateau confusion | Partial | Correct onset/recovery labels, per-sample/event/delay reporting and capacity/weighting experiments. No redundant frozen-count feature or blanket debounce was added. | FROZEN per-sample recall remains poor. Window history and legitimate plateaus remain ambiguous; the harder corpus is not directly comparable with the earlier easy test. |
+| A5: correct evaluation targets | Fixed (software); field validation pending | All ten classes, accuracy/balanced accuracy/macro-F1, binary accuracy, confusion matrices and per-type event/delay results. Integrated evaluation uses raw stimuli, real exported weights and compiled rules. | Event hits may have the wrong type or already be active at onset; typed counts, misses and false alarms are reported. Short integrated sessions do not warm the LSTM. |
+| A6: capacity/regularization/server opinion | Fixed experiment; ESP32 measurement pending | Four MLP configurations share splits/seeds; validation consistency retains weighted 64-32. Larger resampling and stronger regularization/longer patience are experimental artifacts, not deployed settings. Boosting/blend comparisons and native sizeof/timing are recorded. | No >98% per-sample claim. Alpha/patience are a joint experiment. ESP32 linked flash size and on-device inference are unmeasured. |
+| A7: LSTM threshold/fusion | Partial | Shared/per-profile percentile CLI, validation-derived thresholds and precision-recall sweep tables. Continuous score fusion is implemented; tests check continuity and priority. | TP/TPH recall remains limited. Fusion's operational accuracy gain on long held-out multi-station sessions is unmeasured. |
+| B1: traversal/write authentication | Fixed (software), explicit local compatibility scope | `main.py` serves only `/` and `/assets`; tests reject traversal, cross-origin writes, untrusted hosts and tokenless telemetry/reset. | Frozen UI simulation/evaluation POSTs have no token. Opening `/` from loopback issues a token-derived HttpOnly session restricted to these two actions. Remote writes require `X-Station-Token`. This is the documented local compatibility exception, not an anonymous remote write route. |
+| B2: misleading normal/confidence | Partial | API exposes warming/unavailable/missing-data states, range overrides, availability and score-kind text. Temporal, API and formatter tests cover these. | Frozen cards still contain confidence/probability/stable labels and ignore new flags. Legacy confidence is zero plus explanatory text, not 97%. Full visual semantics require frontend changes. |
+| B3: invalid benchmark | Fixed (software) | Real feature pipeline/exported MLP in `local_reference.py`; CLI requires compiled C++ rules. Simulator faults alter raw channels. Explanation coverage and normal success are computed. Native parity and simulation tests pass. | Dashboard can use a parity-tested Python rule fallback without g++; metadata identifies it. Physical health/recovery/pose are outside this benchmark. |
+| B4: pandas datetime units | Fixed (software) | Explicit `.values.astype('datetime64[ns]').astype('int64')/1e9`; requirements support pandas 2.x/3.x. Targeted tests passed under both versions. | Runtime versions and host load affect reproducibility; Python 3.12 is documented. |
+| B5: LSTM cadence/gaps | Fixed (software) | Contiguous 20-row one-minute training windows, stride one; completed minute snapshots live; gap/session resets verified in temporal tests. | Original CSV acquisition provenance is unverified. |
+| B6: faults called weather | Fixed guards; field discrimination partial | Equipment/pose/data-loss/range take precedence. Spatial requires known location, same source, fresh/aligned readings, two neighbours and matching direction/magnitude on two channels. Spatial/precedence tests pass. | Held-out genuine-weather sessions still generate false alerts; guards do not establish field accuracy. |
+| B7: humidity disables TP | Fixed (software) | Ready TP stays active until the TPH sequence is complete; temporal tests verify transition and gaps. | Physical sensor availability still needs verification. |
+| B8: zero placeholders/charts/time | Partial due to frontend freeze | Canonical nullable observations, value/availability fields, acquisition time and gap metadata. Legacy unavailable display values use em dashes. Raw/stored packets remain separate. Formatter/API/browser tests pass. | Original charts filter invalid points, join gaps and plot by index. Backend metadata cannot fix rendering. Valid numeric types remain numeric; unavailable display sentinels are documented. |
+| B9: stale/simulator hardware status | Partial due to frontend freeze | Source, age, freshness/reporting tracked; stale sensor validity/ML processing false, simulation status explicit. Registry/API/browser checks pass. | Original hardware headings/prose remain; source/status must be read. No new MPU or source-selection page. |
+| B10: duplicate/old packets | Fixed backend software; device integration needs hardware | Boot ID, sequence, acquisition time/age in firmware; idempotent identity, ordering/freshness guards and archive-only handling in storage. Duplicate/old/reboot/unknown-time/source tests pass. Original database records preserved. | Real NTP, millis wrap, reboot timing and LoRa gateway identity need device tests. Historical decisions are not retroactively certified. |
+| B11: volatile backlog/alarm delay | Implemented; needs ESP32 build/hardware | Bounded LittleFS backlog, flushed temp write/rename, parsed acknowledgement before deletion, drop counters, latest-critical queue, HTTP/LoRa priority and nonblocking Wi-Fi retry. Existing/corrupt flash is not automatically erased. | LittleFS, FreeRTOS, acknowledgement loss, flash capacity/wear/power cuts, RAM pressure and LoRa are outside portable tests. Capacity eviction is counted. LoRa transmission is not a gateway acknowledgement. |
+| B12: risk as probability | Partial due to frontend freeze | API health index/heuristic kind; link backlog does not add physical risk. Explanations disclose uncalibrated scores. | Frozen risk/probability labels remain. No calibrated horizon or failure percentage. |
+| B13: recovery/trusted baseline | Fixed portable logic; needs hardware | Indefinite capped exponential retries, three valid reads; baseline promotion after three accepted observations, separate expiring estimates never marked valid. Plain-g++ recovery/trusted tests pass. | Actual resets and sustained readings require attached sensors. |
+| B14: inaccurate documentation | Fixed for active project | Active docs describe real classes/features/model/scopes; `make_repair_report.py` derives scores from command artifacts. | Historical audit/legacy addition retain their context; frozen static UI text is unchanged. |
+| B15: MPU addition | Software/core tests; needs hardware | Checked identity/reset/readback/ranges/read length, consistent 100 kHz bus, persistent pose calibration, diagnostics, `I2CSCAN`/`SENSORSRESET`; portable position tests pass. Legacy reapplication guarded. | ESP32 build stopped at failed toolchain downloads, not a compiler pass. Chip ID, mounting, persistence, tilt, bus/reset and recovery need physical tests. |
+| B16: stale dist | Intentionally preserved; serving verified | All ORIGINAL frontend files byte-identical. Browser confirms original HTML served, pages/actions load and no page errors. | Source/dist staleness is not repaired because changes are prohibited. |
+
+## Evidence map
+
+- `docs/INVENTORY.md`, `docs/ARCHIVE_DIFF_ALL.tsv`: ORIGINAL versus REFERENCE before edits.
+- `docs/API_COMPATIBILITY.md`: frozen paths/fields, auth and null constraints identified before repair.
+- `docs/REPAIR_PLAN.md`: finding-to-file plan.
+- `docs/VALIDATION.md`, `docs/verification/`: commands, logs, screenshots, hashes and build limitation.
+- `edge_training/artifacts/*metrics.json`, manifests and checkpoints: training/audit evidence.
+- `backend/models/*metrics.json`: integrated, LSTM and native measurements.
+- `CHANGESET.diff`: complete unified text changes relative to ORIGINAL; full binary artifacts supplied and hashed.
+- `CHANGES.md`: every changed/added/removed deliverable file and purpose. Environments/caches are packaging exclusions, not source repairs.
+
+This output preserves the frozen frontend while leaving incompatible UI requests partial. It does not claim zero false alarms, calibrated confidence, field accuracy, an ESP32 compile pass or physical test completion.
